1.  **`std::max(nums[i], max_ending_here + nums[i])`**: This is the core logic.
    *   If `max_ending_here` is positive, adding `nums[i]` makes it larger, so we keep extending.
    *   If `max_ending_here` is negative, adding `nums[i]` makes it smaller than just taking `nums[i]` alone, so we reset the subarray starting at index `i`.
